{{!
    @template theme_ismos/classtimes

    When a course's classes are, in the viewer's Moodle time zone. The browser rewrites it in the visitor's own time zone
    (theme_ismos/classtimes); without JavaScript the server text, which names its UTC offset, stays.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * form - "long" (course page: full day names and end time) or "short" (cards: short names and start time)
    * text - The line as rendered by the server
    * slots - JSON list of the next class of each weekday: start (timestamp), duration (seconds) and once (one-off)
    * yourtime - "your time"
    * yourtimein - "your time, {$a}", the browser puts the place in {$a}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "form": "long",
        "text": "Tuesday & Thursday, 17:00-18:30 (UTC-3)",
        "slots": "[{\"start\":1794945600,\"duration\":5400,\"once\":false},{\"start\":1795118400,\"duration\":5400,\"once\":false}]",
        "yourtime": "your time",
        "yourtimein": "your time, {$a}"
    }
}}
<span class="ismos-classtimes" data-ismos-classtimes="{{form}}" data-slots="{{slots}}" data-yourtime="{{yourtime}}" data-yourtimein="{{yourtimein}}">{{text}}</span>
{{#js}}
require(['theme_ismos/classtimes'], function(classtimes) {
    classtimes.init();
});
{{/js}}
